---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of business"
  description="Quotation, access, payment and certification terms for Kilbride Electrical."
>
  <div class="page-head">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Terms</p>
      <h1 class="page-head__title">How we quote and deliver work.</h1>
    </div>
  </div>

  <article class="container prose">
    <p class="meta">Last reviewed 7 November 2026</p>

    <h2>Quotations</h2>
    <p>
      A quotation is based on the drawings, access and existing installation visible at survey.
      It stays open for 30 days. Where a survey reveals concealed conditions — asbestos, damaged
      containment, an undocumented supply — we stop and agree a variation before continuing.
    </p>

    <h2>Programme and access</h2>
    <p>
      The client provides safe access, a secure store for materials, and the electrical isolation
      windows recorded in the method statement. Delays caused by access or by other trades move
      the programme by the same period.
    </p>

    <h2>Payment</h2>
    <p>
      Unless the quotation says otherwise, payment is 30 days from invoice. Stage payments apply to
      work longer than six weeks. We may suspend work on an account more than 30 days overdue
      after written notice.
    </p>

    <h2>Certification</h2>
    <p>
      Completed installation work is tested and certified to IS 10101:2020. Certificates are issued
      in the client's name. Work in Northern Ireland is certified to BS 7671. Certification is not
      issued where another contractor has altered or connected to our installation without our
      written agreement.
    </p>

    <h2>Liability and insurance</h2>
    <p>
      We hold public liability insurance of {''}
      <strong>€10m</strong> and employer's liability cover as required by law. Our liability is
      limited to the contract value except where the law does not allow that limit. We do not
      accept liability for loss caused by a supply or installation we did not design, install or
      maintain.
    </p>

    <h2>Retention of title</h2>
    <p>
      Materials remain our property until paid for in full. This does not affect the client's right
      to use a completed and certified installation.
    </p>

    <h2>Disputes</h2>
    <p>
      Raise a concern with the contracts manager first; we will respond within five working days.
      Irish law governs these terms and the courts of Ireland have jurisdiction.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
